The program counts "complete substrings" (LeetCode 2953). Since the word is a single run of identical characters (all 'a', adjacent differences = 0 ≤ 2), it forms one segment. With k = 1, only i = 1 (window length 1) ever satisfies `freq[1] == 1` — every length-1 window qualifies, and no longer window can (counts would exceed 1). For i ≥ 2, `freq[1]` is always 0 ≠ i. Thus the answer equals the length of the word, which is 1000 'a' characters.

The exact stdout text is `1000` followed by a newline.
